 "title": "Doomsday: Friday 13 November 2026",
 "scenes": [
  {
   "narration": "In 1960, three scientists published an equation in Science magazine. Its title: Doomsday, Friday, 13 November, 2026. That is tomorrow.",
   "background": {
    "type": "world3d"
   },
   "elements": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Science, 1960",
     "x": 0.5,
     "y": 0.13,
     "size": 0.042,
     "color": "#ffffff",
     "bg": "#14181f",
     "bg_alpha": 0.9,
     "style": "label",
     "stroke": false,
     "enter": "pop",
     "at": 0.2,
     "until": 99
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "DOOMSDAY: FRIDAY 13 NOV 2026",
     "x": 0.5,
     "y": 0.2,
     "size": 0.05,
     "color": "#ffffff",
     "bg": "#c62828",
     "bg_alpha": 0.9,
     "style": "label",
     "stroke": false,
     "enter": "pop",
     "at_word": "Doomsday,"
    }
   ],
   "id": "s1"
  },
  {
   "narration": "Not an asteroid. Not a war. Us. The maths said the human population was growing faster and faster, and on that Friday the number of people on Earth would reach infinity.",
   "background": {
    "type": "world3d"
   },
   "elements": [
    {
     "type": "counter",
     "from": 0.3,
     "to": 3.0,
     "prefix": "",
     "suffix": " billion in 1960",
     "grouping": "western",
     "decimals": 1,
     "count_dur": 3.0,
     "x": 0.5,
     "y": 0.13,
     "size": 0.05,
     "color": "#ffd54a",
     "bg": "#14181f",
     "bg_alpha": 0.85,
     "style": "label",
     "stroke": false,
     "enter": "pop",
     "at_word": "growing",
     "until": 99
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Population: infinity",
     "x": 0.5,
     "y": 0.2,
     "size": 0.05,
     "color": "#ffffff",
     "bg": "#c62828",
     "bg_alpha": 0.9,
     "style": "label",
     "stroke": false,
     "enter": "pop",
     "at_word": "infinity."
    }
   ],
   "id": "s2"
  },
  {
   "narration": "So let's play it out. Suppose the equation was right.",
   "background": {
    "type": "world3d"
   },
   "elements": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "What if it were true?",
     "x": 0.5,
     "y": 0.13,
     "size": 0.044,
     "color": "#ffffff",
     "bg": "#14181f",
     "bg_alpha": 0.9,
     "style": "label",
     "stroke": false,
     "enter": "pop",
     "at": 0.2
    }
   ],
   "id": "s3"
  },
  {
   "narration": "By the 1990s there are 12 billion of us. Cities swallow the farms, the forests, the rivers. There is nowhere left to grow food.",
   "background": {
    "type": "world3d"
   },
   "elements": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "1990s",
     "x": 0.5,
     "y": 0.13,
     "size": 0.042,
     "color": "#ffffff",
     "bg": "#14181f",
     "bg_alpha": 0.9,
     "style": "label",
     "stroke": false,
     "enter": "pop",
     "at": 0.2,
     "until": 99
    },
    {
     "type": "counter",
     "from": 6,
     "to": 12,
     "prefix": "",
     "suffix": " billion people",
     "grouping": "western",
     "decimals": 1,
     "count_dur": 2.5,
     "x": 0.5,
     "y": 0.22,
     "size": 0.05,
     "color": "#ffd54a",
     "bg": "#14181f",
     "bg_alpha": 0.85,
     "style": "label",
     "stroke": false,
     "enter": "pop",
     "at_word": "12",
     "until": 99
    }
   ],
   "id": "s4"
  },
  {
   "narration": "By 2010, 60 billion. The oceans are fished empty. Water is rationed by the cup. Every roof, every road, every field is covered in people.",
   "background": {
    "type": "world3d"
   },
   "elements": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "2010",
     "x": 0.5,
     "y": 0.13,
     "size": 0.042,
